 "_about": "Held-out v4 (2026-10-01), written to measure classic *with* the replacement cue (pipeline.change.marks_replacement) on sentences it was not written from. Written and frozen BEFORE marks_replacement or any model was run on it; no rule, prompt or threshold may be chosen by looking at its failures. Authored by the author of the cue, so not independent. To keep it from being shaped to the rule: mixed register (48% of current statements end in a spoken form such as -요/-죠), reversed_alternative with 8 of 20 statements containing a swap verb the cue knows and the rest phrased otherwise (도입, 말고, 대신, -로 가요, -로 정했어요, 쓰기로, 돌린다), and parameter changes phrased with the same verbs a team really uses (옮기다, 바꾸다, 교체) at natural frequency. Cases whose label could be argued both ways (a state toggle such as free -> paid) were not written. Labels follow dataset.py.",
